no flag requests no geometry, so the renderer picks exactly as it did before the flag existed: true
and the machine is not consulted to decide that: true
the header says so rather than leaving the geometry unstated: true
--tile= is taken verbatim, in rm,rn,lanes order: true
a verbatim geometry consults the machine too, once: true
the header names the requested geometry and says it was requested: true
--rn= consults the machine exactly once: true
--rn= keeps the column count it was given, and derives the rest: true
the rows are the renderer's cap, not a constant restated here: true
the width is the widest the file renders at this element size, the head of the ladder: true
on a site with the rows and columns to spare, the derived geometry is one check accepts: true
a geometry no 512-column site can honour is still handed to the renderer, not pre-rejected: true
neither spelling is taken on a backend with no register-tiled rendering to describe: true
a geometry that reaches no schedule in this run is refused, naming it and why: true
and a run that requested nothing has nothing to refuse: true
--tile= together with --rn= is refused, naming both: true
a malformed geometry is refused by name, where it is read: true
a count that would wrap the width or the live-register arithmetic is refused, naming the rule: true
the parser never refuses an rm that Register_tile.check would take: true
a requested geometry that reached no Tile_mma is reported as not measured: true
a requested geometry that reached one is not: true
a run that requested nothing never reports it, at any statement count: true
whitespace inside the triple is stripped rather than failing to parse: true
machine consulted 15 time(s) over the whole run
